IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate

-- Code of Alabama 1975, Title 40, Chapter 18 (Income Taxes) -- the individual income tax of a resident of Alabama.
--
-- Edition: the text ALISON served on 2026-10-20, as deposited at
--   ../../registers/source-bundle/ala-code-40-18-art1.txt      (Article 1, ss 40-18-1 to 40-18-62)
--   ../../registers/source-bundle/ala-code-40-18-art2-div1.txt (Article 2 Division 1, ss 40-18-70 to 40-18-86)
-- ALISON publishes no 'current through' date. Its own notes say s 40-18-14 was amended by Act 2026-551 (effective
-- 1 May 2026) and s 40-18-15 by Act 2026-604 (effective 1 October 2026), and that the text shown may not include those
-- amendments. Neither Act is deposited. See NOTES.md findings 1 and 2.
--
-- In: s 40-18-2(a)(1), (b) (who is taxed; the residence presumption), s 40-18-5 (rates), s 40-18-15(b)(4) (the optional
-- standard deduction for tax years beginning after 31 December 2021), s 40-18-15(c) (the deduction for federal income tax),
-- s 40-18-15.1 (taxable income), s 40-18-19(a)(8), (9)a, d, e, (13) (personal and dependent exemptions; the $6,000
-- retirement income exemption at 65), s 40-18-19.1(b), (d) (severance and unemployment compensation after downsizing),
-- s 40-18-27(a), (c) (who must file; by when), s 40-18-42(a) (when the balance is due), s 40-18-50 (the penalty for not
-- filing), s 40-18-73(a), (c), (g) (the Form A-4 withholding certificate), s 40-18-75(a) (the wage statement).
--
-- Out: gross income and adjusted gross income themselves (ss 40-18-14, 40-18-14.2: Alabama computes its own AGI, item by
-- item, mostly by reference to the Internal Revenue Code; the person states the figure); the itemised deductions of
-- s 40-18-15(a) (stated as one total by the person who itemises); nonresidents (s 40-18-19(b) and s 40-18-15(e) prorate:
-- `not covered`); tax years before 2022 (`not covered`); the other credits and exemptions; estimated tax (s 40-18-80, which
-- borrows 26 U.S.C. 6654); corporations, estates and trusts.
--
-- Federal links (not imported: the stable l4 cannot IMPORT across folders): s 40-18-15(c) federal income tax is the amount
-- the person paid or accrued (subjects/us/internal-revenue-code-of-1986); "head of family" is "head of household" in
-- 26 U.S.C. 2(b) (s 40-18-1(15)), asked as a fact.
--
-- BASELINE ENCODING, written straight from the deposited text from the seat of the individual taxpayer. Expected values in
-- the case file are hand-written. No pipeline, no independent test pass, no human gate. NOT FOR USE AS TAX ADVICE.

§ `Code of Alabama 1975, Title 40, Chapter 18 -- the individual income tax`

§§ `What this encoding does not cover`

DECLARE `Why not covered` IS ONE OF
    -- s 40-18-15(b)(4) and s 40-18-19(a)(9)d, e apply "for tax years beginning after December 31, 2021"; the earlier
    -- tables are in the text but are not encoded
    `this encoding computes the tax for tax years from 2022 only`
    -- s 40-18-2(a)(6), s 40-18-15(e), s 40-18-19(b): nonresidents are taxed on Alabama-source income and their deductions
    -- and exemptions are prorated by a ratio this encoding does not compute
    `the tax of a nonresident individual is not encoded`

DECLARE `Answer` IS ONE OF
    `answered`    HAS `amount`  IS A NUMBER
    `not covered` HAS `because` IS A `Why not covered`

§§ `Filing status`

-- The categories s 40-18-5 and s 40-18-15(b)(4) use. "Head of family" has the meaning of "head of household" in
-- 26 U.S.C. 2(b) (s 40-18-1(15)); it is asked as a fact.
DECLARE `Filing status` IS ONE OF
    `single`
    `head of family`
    `married filing separate return`
    `married filing joint return`

§§ `s 40-18-2 -- who is taxed; residence`

-- s 40-18-2(b): "Every natural person domiciled in the State of Alabama, and every other natural person who maintains a
-- permanent place of abode within the state or spends in the aggregate more than seven months of the income year within
-- the state, shall be presumed to be residing within the state". A presumption (NOTES.md finding 6).
GIVEN `domiciled in Alabama`                         IS A BOOLEAN
      `maintains a permanent place of abode in Alabama` IS A BOOLEAN
      `months spent in Alabama in the income year`   IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `presumed to be residing in Alabama` IF
        `domiciled in Alabama`
    OR  `maintains a permanent place of abode in Alabama`
    OR  `months spent in Alabama in the income year` GREATER THAN 7

§§ `s 40-18-15(b)(4) -- the optional standard deduction (tax years beginning after 31 December 2021)`

-- Each filing status has a full amount below an AGI threshold, a reduction "for each" step of AGI "in excess of" the
-- threshold, and a floor. "For each $500" is read as each complete $500 (NOTES.md finding 3).
GIVEN `full amount` IS A NUMBER, `threshold` IS A NUMBER, `reduction` IS A NUMBER, `step` IS A NUMBER, `floor amount` IS A NUMBER, `adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the phased standard deduction` MEANS
    IF `adjusted gross income` AT MOST `threshold`
    THEN `full amount`
    ELSE max `floor amount` (`full amount` MINUS (`reduction` TIMES (FLOOR ((`adjusted gross income` MINUS `threshold`) DIVIDED BY `step`))))

GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`, `adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the optional standard deduction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `status`
    -- (4)a: $8,500 below $25,500; less $175 for each $500 over; not less than $5,000
    WHEN `married filing joint return`    THEN `the phased standard deduction` 8500 25500 175 500 5000 `adjusted gross income`
    -- (4)b: $4,250 below $12,750; less $88 for each $250 over; not less than $2,500
    WHEN `married filing separate return` THEN `the phased standard deduction` 4250 12750 88 250 2500 `adjusted gross income`
    -- (4)c: $5,200 below $25,500; less $135 for each $500 over; not less than $2,500
    WHEN `head of family`                 THEN `the phased standard deduction` 5200 25500 135 500 2500 `adjusted gross income`
    -- (4)d: $3,000 below $25,500; less $25 for each $500 over; not less than $2,500
    WHEN `single`                         THEN `the phased standard deduction` 3000 25500 25 500 2500 `adjusted gross income`

§§ `s 40-18-19(a)(8) -- the personal exemption`

-- "a single person or a married person not living with a spouse": $1,500; "a head of a family or a married person living
-- with a spouse": $3,000; spouses living together get one $3,000 against their aggregate income, "and in case they make
-- separate returns each spouse must claim a personal exemption of one thousand five hundred dollars ($1,500)". Read by
-- filing status: a joint return gets $3,000 whether or not the spouses live together, since two spouses apart would each
-- have $1,500 (NOTES.md finding 8).
GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the personal exemption` MEANS
    CONSIDER `status`
    WHEN `single`                         THEN 1500
    WHEN `head of family`                 THEN 3000
    WHEN `married filing joint return`    THEN 3000
    WHEN `married filing separate return` THEN 1500

§§ `s 40-18-19(a)(9) -- the dependent exemption`

-- For tax years beginning after 31 December 2021: $1,000 a dependent at AGI up to $50,000 (d.), $500 above $50,000 and up
-- to $100,000 (e.); above $100,000 only the $300 of paragraph a. is left (NOTES.md finding 4). A "dependent" is a relative of
-- the listed kinds over half of whose support came from the taxpayer; asked as a count.
GIVEN `adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the exemption for each dependent` MEANS
    IF `adjusted gross income` AT MOST 50000
    THEN 1000
    ELSE IF `adjusted gross income` AT MOST 100000
         THEN 500
         ELSE 300

§§ `s 40-18-19(a)(13) -- the retirement income exemption at 65`

-- "Beginning January 1, 2023, the first six thousand dollars ($6,000) of taxable retirement income", claimed only "by
-- individual taxpayers who are 65 years of age or older". Applied to each spouse on a joint return separately (finding 5).
GIVEN `tax year` IS A NUMBER, `aged 65 or older` IS A BOOLEAN, `taxable retirement income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the retirement income exemption of one taxpayer` MEANS
    IF `tax year` AT LEAST 2023 AND `aged 65 or older`
    THEN min 6000 `taxable retirement income`
    ELSE 0

§§ `s 40-18-19.1 -- severance and unemployment compensation after administrative downsizing`

-- (b): for tax years beginning after 31 December 2019, up to $50,000 a year "received as severance, unemployment
-- compensation, or termination pay, or as income from a supplemental income plan" by an employee who "as a result of
-- administrative downsizing, is terminated, laid-off, fired, or displaced"; limited to the actual payments.
-- (d): not where the termination "is due to misconduct".
GIVEN `lost the job as a result of administrative downsizing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `terminated for misconduct`                            IS A BOOLEAN
      `severance and unemployment compensation received`      IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the s 40-18-19.1 exempt amount` MEANS
    IF `lost the job as a result of administrative downsizing` AND (NOT `terminated for misconduct`)
    THEN min 50000 `severance and unemployment compensation received`
    ELSE 0

§§ `s 40-18-15.1 -- taxable income`

-- One resident individual's (or one married couple's joint) return for one tax year. Adjusted gross income is the
-- Alabama figure under s 40-18-14.2, stated by the taxpayer, with any s 40-18-19.1 amount already left out.
DECLARE `Return` HAS
    `tax year`                                   IS A NUMBER
    `resident`                                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `status`                                     IS A `Filing status`
    `adjusted gross income`                      IS A NUMBER
    `itemises deductions`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `itemised deductions`                        IS A NUMBER
    `federal income tax paid or accrued`         IS A NUMBER
    `dependents`                                 IS A NUMBER
    `taxpayer aged 65 or older`                  IS A BOOLEAN
    `taxpayer's taxable retirement income`       IS A NUMBER
    `spouse aged 65 or older`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `spouse's taxable retirement income`         IS A NUMBER

-- s 40-18-15(b)(1): the optional standard deduction is taken "in lieu of" the itemised deductions; the taxpayer elects.
GIVEN r IS A `Return`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the deduction in place of itemising, or the itemised total` MEANS
    IF r's `itemises deductions`
    THEN r's `itemised deductions`
    ELSE `the optional standard deduction` (r's `status`) (r's `adjusted gross income`)

GIVEN r IS A `Return`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the exemptions` MEANS
        `the personal exemption` (r's `status`)
    PLUS (r's `dependents` TIMES `the exemption for each dependent` (r's `adjusted gross income`))
    PLUS `the retirement income exemption of one taxpayer` (r's `tax year`) (r's `taxpayer aged 65 or older`) (r's `taxpayer's taxable retirement income`)
    PLUS `the spouse's retirement income exemption` r

GIVEN r IS A `Return`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the spouse's retirement income exemption` MEANS
    IF r's `status` EQUALS `married filing joint return`
    THEN `the retirement income exemption of one taxpayer` (r's `tax year`) (r's `spouse aged 65 or older`) (r's `spouse's taxable retirement income`)
    ELSE 0

-- "gross income ... less the deductions allowed to individuals by this chapter" (s 40-18-15.1), with the federal income
-- tax deduction of s 40-18-15(c) and the s 40-18-19 exemptions; never below nil.
GIVEN r IS A `Return`
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the taxable income` MEANS
    max 0 (r's `adjusted gross income`
           MINUS `the deduction in place of itemising, or the itemised total` r
           MINUS r's `federal income tax paid or accrued`
           MINUS `the exemptions` r)

§§ `s 40-18-5 -- the tax on individuals`

GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`, `taxable income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the tax on taxable income` MEANS
    IF `status` EQUALS `married filing joint return`
    -- (2): 2% to $1,000; 4% over $1,000 to $6,000; 5% over $6,000
    THEN `the bracket tax` 1000 6000 `taxable income`
    -- (1): single, head of family, married filing separately: 2% to $500; 4% over $500 to $3,000; 5% over $3,000
    ELSE `the bracket tax` 500 3000 `taxable income`

GIVEN `first band top` IS A NUMBER, `second band top` IS A NUMBER, `taxable income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the bracket tax` MEANS
        (2%  TIMES min `taxable income` `first band top`)
    PLUS (4% TIMES max 0 (min `taxable income` `second band top` MINUS `first band top`))
    PLUS (5% TIMES max 0 (`taxable income` MINUS `second band top`))

GIVEN r IS A `Return`
GIVETH AN `Answer`
`the income tax` MEANS
    IF r's `tax year` LESS THAN 2022
    THEN `not covered` `this encoding computes the tax for tax years from 2022 only`
    ELSE IF NOT (r's `resident`)
         THEN `not covered` `the tax of a nonresident individual is not encoded`
         ELSE `answered` (`the tax on taxable income` (r's `status`) (`the taxable income` r))

§§ `s 40-18-27 -- who must file`

-- (a): every taxpayer "having gross income before the deductions ... exceeding the sum of the allowable standard deduction
-- as provided in Section 40-18-15 and the personal exemption as provided in Section 40-18-19, as allowed for his or her
-- respective filing status, shall each year file". The standard deduction is taken at the taxpayer's AGI (finding 7).
GIVEN `status` IS A `Filing status`, `gross income` IS A NUMBER, `adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `required to file a return` IF
    `gross income` GREATER THAN
        (`the optional standard deduction` `status` `adjusted gross income` PLUS `the personal exemption` `status`)

§§ `Duties with deadlines`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the taxpayer`
    `the employee`
    `the employer`

DECLARE `Act` IS ONE OF
    `file the return with the Department of Revenue`
    `pay the balance of the tax`
    `furnish a signed Alabama Form A-4`
    `withhold using no exemptions`
    `claim more withholding exemptions than the employee is entitled to`
    `submit a new withholding exemption certificate`
    `furnish the written wage statement`

-- s 40-18-27(a), (c): the taxpayer required to file "shall each year file", by "the same date as the corresponding federal
-- income tax returns are required to be filed"; `days to the due date` counts from the end of the tax year, extended by any
-- extension the department grants (not more than six months, except for taxpayers abroad). s 40-18-50: failing to file in
-- time is a misdemeanour, fined $10 to $1,000.
GIVEN `who` IS A `Party`, `days to the due date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the duty to file` `who` `days to the due date` MEANS
    PARTY `who`
    MUST  `file the return with the Department of Revenue`
    WITHIN `days to the due date`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `who` BECAUSE "s 40-18-50: no return within the time allowed; a misdemeanour, fine of $10 to $1,000"

-- s 40-18-42(a): the balance of the tax after withholding and estimated payments "shall be due and payable at the same time
-- as the due date of an original return".
GIVEN `who` IS A `Party`, `days to the due date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the duty to pay the balance` `who` `days to the due date` MEANS
    PARTY `who`
    MUST  `pay the balance of the tax`
    WITHIN `days to the due date`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `who` BECAUSE "s 40-18-42(a): balance of tax not paid by the due date of the original return"

-- s 40-18-73(a): every employee, "on or before the date of commencement of employment", shall furnish a signed Alabama
-- withholding exemption certificate (Form A-4; a federal W-4 will not do, (b)). (c): if not, "the employer must withhold
-- on such employee's wages using no exemptions". Days count from the start of employment.
GIVEN `employee` IS A `Party`, `employer` IS A `Party`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the duty to furnish a Form A-4` `employee` `employer` MEANS
    PARTY `employee`
    MUST  `furnish a signed Alabama Form A-4`
    WITHIN 0
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST
        PARTY `employer`
        MUST  `withhold using no exemptions`

-- s 40-18-73(a): the number claimed "in no event shall exceed the number to which the employee is entitled"; an employee
-- who inflates it "shall pay a penalty of five hundred dollars ($500)".
GIVEN `employee` IS A `Party`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the prohibition on inflating exemptions` `employee` MEANS
    PARTY `employee`
    SHANT `claim more withholding exemptions than the employee is entitled to`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `employee` BECAUSE "s 40-18-73(a): exemptions inflated on Form A-4; penalty of $500 under s 40-29-75"

-- s 40-18-73(g): "Whenever the number of exemptions of an employee either increases or decreases, the employee shall submit
-- to the employer a new exemption certificate". No time is stated, so no WITHIN.
GIVEN `employee` IS A `Party`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the duty to update the certificate` `employee` MEANS
    PARTY `employee`
    MUST  `submit a new withholding exemption certificate`

-- s 40-18-75(a): the employer that withheld shall furnish each employee a written statement of wages and tax withheld "on or
-- before January 31 of the succeeding year, or, if his employment is terminated before the close of such calendar year,
-- within 30 days from the day on which the last payment of remuneration is made". (c): the department may extend the time
-- by not more than 30 days.
GIVEN `employer` IS A `Party`, `days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Act`
`the duty to give the wage statement` `employer` `days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `employer`
    MUST  `furnish the written wage statement`
    WITHIN `days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST  BREACH BY `employer` BECAUSE "s 40-18-75(a): wage statement not furnished in time"

GIVEN `calendar year` IS A NUMBER, `employment terminated before the year ended` IS A BOOLEAN, `day of the last payment of wages` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day for the wage statement` MEANS
    IF `employment terminated before the year ended`
    THEN `day of the last payment of wages` PLUS 30
    ELSE Date 31 1 (`calendar year` PLUS 1)

-- =====================================================================================================================
§ `Questions for the taxpayer`
-- The seat: the individual Alabama taxpayer (and, for withholding, the same person as an employee). Each question is
-- derived from the rules above.

§§ `Am I an Alabama resident?`

@export Am I presumed to be residing in Alabama for Alabama income tax (Ala. Code s 40-18-2(b))?
GIVEN `I am domiciled in Alabama` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Is Alabama your domicile (your permanent legal home)?
      `I keep a permanent home in Alabama` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Do you maintain a permanent place of abode in Alabama?
      `months I spent in Alabama` IS A NUMBER @desc In total, how many months of the tax year did you spend in Alabama?
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Am I presumed to be an Alabama resident` MEANS
    `presumed to be residing in Alabama` `I am domiciled in Alabama` `I keep a permanent home in Alabama` `months I spent in Alabama`

§§ `Must I file?`

@export Must I file an Alabama individual income tax return for the year (Ala. Code s 40-18-27(a))?
GIVEN `my filing status` IS A `Filing status` @desc Your filing status: single, head of family, married filing separate return or married filing joint return
      `my gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your gross income for the year before any deductions, in US dollars
      `my adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Alabama adjusted gross income for the year, in US dollars
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Must I file an Alabama return` MEANS
    `required to file a return` `my filing status` `my gross income` `my adjusted gross income`

§§ `How much is my tax?`

@export What is my Alabama optional standard deduction for a tax year from 2022 (Ala. Code s 40-18-15(b)(4))?
GIVEN `my filing status` IS A `Filing status` @desc Your filing status: single, head of family, married filing separate return or married filing joint return
      `my adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Alabama adjusted gross income for the year, in US dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is my Alabama standard deduction` MEANS
    `the optional standard deduction` `my filing status` `my adjusted gross income`

@export What are my Alabama personal and dependent exemptions for a tax year from 2022 (Ala. Code s 40-18-19(a)(8), (9))?
GIVEN `my filing status` IS A `Filing status` @desc Your filing status: single, head of family, married filing separate return or married filing joint return
      `my adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Alabama adjusted gross income for the year, in US dollars
      `my dependents` IS A NUMBER @desc How many relatives, other than your spouse, received over half of their support from you this year?
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What are my Alabama personal and dependent exemptions` MEANS
    `the personal exemption` `my filing status` PLUS (`my dependents` TIMES `the exemption for each dependent` `my adjusted gross income`)

@export How much of my severance or unemployment pay is exempt from Alabama income tax after a downsizing (Ala. Code s 40-18-19.1)?
GIVEN `I lost my job in a downsizing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you terminated, laid off, fired or displaced as a result of administrative downsizing?
      `I was terminated for misconduct` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Was your termination due to misconduct?
      `my severance and unemployment pay` IS A NUMBER @desc Severance, unemployment compensation, termination pay and supplemental income plan payments you received this year, in US dollars
GIVETH A NUMBER
`How much of my severance or unemployment pay is exempt` MEANS
    `the s 40-18-19.1 exempt amount` `I lost my job in a downsizing` `I was terminated for misconduct` `my severance and unemployment pay`

@export How much Alabama income tax do I owe for the year, as a resident individual (Ala. Code ss 40-18-5, 40-18-15, 40-18-19)?
GIVEN `tax year` IS A NUMBER @desc The tax year, e.g. 2025
      `I am an Alabama resident` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Were you an Alabama resident for the whole year?
      `my filing status` IS A `Filing status` @desc Your filing status: single, head of family, married filing separate return or married filing joint return
      `my adjusted gross income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your Alabama adjusted gross income for the year (on a joint return, both spouses'), in US dollars
      `I itemise` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Will you itemise deductions instead of taking the optional standard deduction?
      `my itemised deductions` IS A NUMBER @desc Your itemised deductions under Ala. Code s 40-18-15(a), in US dollars (0 if you do not itemise)
      `my federal income tax` IS A NUMBER @desc Federal income tax you paid or accrued in the year, in US dollars
      `my dependents` IS A NUMBER @desc How many relatives, other than your spouse, received over half of their support from you this year?
      `I am 65 or older` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Are you 65 or older?
      `my taxable retirement income` IS A NUMBER @desc Your taxable retirement income for the year, in US dollars
      `my spouse is 65 or older` IS A BOOLEAN @desc On a joint return: is your spouse 65 or older?
      `my spouse's taxable retirement income` IS A NUMBER @desc On a joint return: your spouse's taxable retirement income, in US dollars
GIVETH AN `Answer`
`How much Alabama income tax do I owe` MEANS
    `the income tax` (`Return` WITH
        `tax year`                             IS `tax year`
        `resident`                             IS `I am an Alabama resident`
        `status`                               IS `my filing status`
        `adjusted gross income`                IS `my adjusted gross income`
        `itemises deductions`                  IS `I itemise`
        `itemised deductions`                  IS `my itemised deductions`
        `federal income tax paid or accrued`   IS `my federal income tax`
        `dependents`                           IS `my dependents`
        `taxpayer aged 65 or older`            IS `I am 65 or older`
        `taxpayer's taxable retirement income` IS `my taxable retirement income`
        `spouse aged 65 or older`              IS `my spouse is 65 or older`
        `spouse's taxable retirement income`   IS `my spouse's taxable retirement income`)

§§ `When I start a job (withholding)`

@export By what day must my employer give me my Alabama wage statement for a calendar year (Ala. Code s 40-18-75(a))?
GIVEN `calendar year` IS A NUMBER @desc The calendar year the wages were paid in
      `my job ended during that year` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Did your employment end before the close of that calendar year?
      `day of my last pay` IS A DATE @desc The day your last wages were paid (used only if the job ended during the year)
GIVETH A DATE
`By when must my employer give me my wage statement` MEANS
    `the last day for the wage statement` `calendar year` `my job ended during that year` `day of my last pay`
